  "_note": "BPM is due on the first registration on a Dutch plate — new or used, from inside the EU or outside it. The base is CO2 and age only: the purchase price never enters it. Where a car has no certified CO2 the Belastingdienst applies a punitive forfait (petrol 550 g/km, diesel 395 g/km for cars first registered from 1 July 2020; 507/356 from 2015; 350/302 from 2009), which is real but so far above any actual car that showing it as an estimate would mislead — we ask for the CO2 instead.",
